# These are executed inside Linux containers and on CI runners. A CRLF
# checkout on Windows puts a carriage return in the shebang, and the container
# fails with a "no such file or directory" that names an interpreter that is
# plainly there. Pin them to LF regardless of core.autocrlf.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*    text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
